# Build-context excludes for `flyctl deploy` / `docker build` (context root = repo root).
# Without this, a local deploy uploads the entire working tree (~31GB: .claude
# worktrees, .venv, node_modules, .next). The Dockerfiles install deps and build
# fresh, so none of the excluded paths are needed in the image. CI builds from a
# clean checkout and never hit the bloat, but local `flyctl deploy` does.
#
# Keep: packages/core/, packages/ui/, fixtures/, knowledge/, docker/ — i.e. only
# the paths the Dockerfiles COPY. Do NOT add those here.

# Version control & agent state
.git
.gitignore
.claude

# Python virtualenvs & tool caches (deps installed fresh in-image)
**/.venv
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/.pytest_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/.ruff_cache

# Node deps & build output (npm ci + next build run in-image)
**/node_modules
packages/ui/.next

# Local runtime data & vector store (live on the Fly volume at runtime)
**/*.db
chroma_db
**/chroma_db

# Secrets & local env — never ship to the build context. The recursive forms
# matter because the monorepo also uses packages/core/.env and
# packages/ui/.env.local.
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/.gworkspace-credentials

# Local company data (gitignored; not needed in the image)
company
**/company

# Editor / OS cruft
.obsidian
.vscode
.idea
.DS_Store
*.log
